# No Native UI Components

Do not use native HTML elements for interactive or styled UI. This project uses the shadcn design system — always compose UI from `@/components/ui/*`.

Reference: [shadcn components](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components)

## Workflow

1. **Check the project first** — look in `apps/web/src/components/ui/` for an existing component.
2. **Pick the best shadcn match** — browse the docs and choose the right primitive (e.g. `Dialog` over a custom modal, `Select` over a raw `<select>`).
3. **Install if missing** — from `apps/web`, run:
   ```bash
   pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>
   ```
4. **Import and use** — `import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"`

## Native → shadcn mapping

| Native | Use instead |
|--------|-------------|
| `<button>` | `Button` |
| `<input>` | `Input` |
| `<textarea>` | `Textarea` |
| `<select>` | `Select` or `Combobox` |
| `<label>` | `Label` + `Field` / `FormLabel` |
| `<a>` styled as button | `Button asChild` + `Link` |
| `<dialog>` / custom modal | `Dialog` or `AlertDialog` |
| `<input type="checkbox">` | `Checkbox` |
| raw toggle | `Switch` or `Toggle` |
| unstyled list/table | `Table` or `DataTable` |
| tooltip via `title` | `Tooltip` |
| dropdown via custom div | `DropdownMenu` or `Popover` |

Semantic-only elements (`<main>`, `<section>`, `<nav>`, `<h1>`–`<h6>`, `<p>`) are fine. The rule targets **interactive and design-system UI**.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — native elements
<button onClick={onSave}>Save</button>
<input value={name} onChange={e => setName(e.target.value)} />
<select value={role} onChange={e => setRole(e.target.value)}>...</select>

// ✅ GOOD — shadcn components
<Button onClick={onSave}>Save</Button>
<Input value={name} onChange={e => setName(e.target.value)} />
<Select value={role} onValueChange={setRole}>...</Select>
```
